  td.num, th.num { text-align: right; font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums; }
  .mono { font-family: ui-monospace, "SFMono-Regular", Consolas, monospace; }
  .card { border: 1px solid #666; border-radius: 6px; padding: .7rem .9rem; margin: 0 0 1rem; break-inside: avoid; page-break-inside: avoid; }
  .tag { display: inline-block; border: 1px solid #111; border-radius: 4px; padding: 0 .35rem; font-size: .75rem; font-weight: 700; margin-left: .4rem; vertical-align: middle; }
  dl { margin: 0; }
  dt { font-weight: 700; margin-top: .5rem; }
  dd { margin: 0 0 0 1rem; }
  footer { margin-top: 2.5rem; padding-top: .6rem; border-top: 1px solid #999; font-size: .85rem; color: #333; }
  @media print { body { margin: 0; max-width: none; } h2 { break-after: avoid; } }
</style></head><body><header><h1>HSU 2026-27</h1><p class="meta">Report generated 2026-10-14</p><p class="note">This is a read-only copy of a swim team plan from Omniswim Suite. It lists each team’s projected and actual points, then the lineup for one team. Open it in any browser. Print it to keep a paper copy or save a PDF.</p></header><section><h2>Team scores</h2><p class="note">Projected points are the app’s estimate from stored times. Actual points are the official totals from the meet results PDF.</p><table><thead><tr><th class="num">Rank</th><th>Team</th><th class="num">Projected points</th><th class="num">Actual points (official)</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td class="num">1</td><td>Henderson State University <span class="tag">Selected team</span></td><td class="num mono">412.5</td><td class="num mono">400.0</td></tr><tr><td class="num">2</td><td>Other University</td><td class="num mono">100.0</td><td class="num mono">—</td></tr></tbody></table></section><section><h2>Lineup: Henderson State University (Men)</h2><p class="meta">Projected team points: 412.5</p><h2>Individual events</h2><div class="card"><h3>Event 4 Men 1000 Yard Freestyle <span class="meta">Round: —</span></h3><table><thead><tr><th>Swimmer</th><th>Class</th><th>Seed time</th><th>Course</th><th class="num">Projected place</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Colton Bennett</td><td>JR</td><td class="mono">9:26.63</td><td>SCY</td><td class="num">—</td></tr><tr><td>Blank Time</td><td>JR</td><td class="mono">—</td><td>SCY</td><td class="num">—</td></tr></tbody></table></div><div class="card"><h3>Event 8 Men 50 Yard Freestyle <span class="meta">Round: —</span></h3><table><thead><tr><th>Swimmer</th><th>Class</th><th>Seed time</th><th>Course</th><th class="num">Projected place</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Fast Fifty</td><td>JR</td><td class="mono">20.95</td><td>SCY</td><td class="num">—</td></tr></tbody></table></div><h2>Relays</h2><div class="card"><h3>Event 42 Men 4x100 Yard Freestyle Relay <span class="meta">Round: A Final</span></h3><p class="meta">Relay time: <span class="mono">3:05.81</span></p><table><thead><tr><th class="num">Leg</th><th>Swimmer</th><th>Leg time</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td class="num">1</td><td>Colin Candebat</td><td class="mono">44.32</td></tr><tr><td class="num">2</td><td>Vitor Sa<span class="tag">Time trial</span></td><td class="mono">45.09</td></tr><tr><td class="num">3</td><td>Vacant</td><td class="mono">—</td></tr><tr><td class="num">4</td><td>Oliver Pozvai</td><td class="mono">44.35</td></tr></tbody></table></div><div class="card"><h3>Event 42 Men 4x100 Yard Freestyle Relay <span class="meta">Round: B Final</span></h3><p class="meta">Relay time: <span class="mono">3:06.60</span></p><table><thead><tr><th class="num">Leg</th><th>Swimmer</th><th>Leg time</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td class="num">1</td><td>Nojus Skirutis</td><td class="mono">46.45</td></tr><tr><td class="num">2</td><td>Gavin Kock<span class="tag">Time trial</span></td><td class="mono">46.53</td></tr><tr><td class="num">3</td><td>Tristen Fergunson</td><td class="mono">46.38</td></tr><tr><td class="num">4</td><td>Colton Bennett</td><td class="mono">47.24</td></tr></tbody></table></div></section><section><h2>Key terms</h2><dl><dt>Dash (—)</dt><dd>The workspace has no value here. It does not mean zero. A swimmer with a dash has no stored time.</dd><dt>Projected points</dt><dd>Points the app expects a team to score if the lineup swims its stored times. It is an estimate, not a result.</dd><dt>Actual points</dt><dd>The official team total printed in the meet results PDF. It is only shown when that PDF was loaded.</dd><dt>Seed time</dt><dd>The time stored for a swimmer in an event. The meet uses it to rank entries.</dd><dt>Course</dt><dd>The pool length of the stored time. SCY is short course yards, SCM is short course meters, LCM is long course meters.</dd><dt>Class</dt><dd>The swimmer’s class year, such as FR, SO, JR or SR.</dd><dt>Round and place</dt><dd>Prelims or finals, and the place the app projects in that round from seed times. A dash means no place is projected.</dd><dt>Relay leg</dt><dd>One swimmer’s part of a relay. Leg 1 swims first.</dd><dt>Time trial</dt><dd>The leg time comes from a time trial swim, not from the meet. The workspace allows this time to fill a relay leg.</dd><dt>Estimate</dt><dd>Nobody swam this relay in the loaded meet. The app built the lineup from individual times, so the relay time is a projection.</dd><dt>Vacant</dt><dd>No swimmer is assigned to this relay leg.</dd></dl></section><footer>Generated by Omniswim Suite from the workspace as saved on 2026-10-14; projections are estimates from published times.</footer></body></html>
